# Skyrim SKSE Plugin Development (CommonLibSSE-NG)

You are developing a native Skyrim Special Edition / Anniversary Edition SKSE plugin using CommonLibSSE-NG.

## Project

- Project root: H:/Nolvus Awakening/PROJECTS/MySkyrimPlugin
- CMake project name: HelloWorld
- Main source file: plugin.cpp
- Precompiled header: PCH.h
- C++ standard: C++23
- vcpkg dependency: commonlibsse-ng
- Target triplet: x64-windows-static-md

## Code Conventions & Architecture

1. Namespaces
   - RE:: — reverse-engineered Skyrim engine classes, forms, structs, and events (e.g. RE::PlayerCharacter, RE::Actor, RE::TESObjectWEAP, RE::ConsoleLog, RE::TESEquipEvent).
   - SKSE:: — plugin lifecycle, interfaces, messaging, trampolines, and logging (e.g. SKSE::GetMessagingInterface(), SKSE::Trampoline, SKSE::Init()).

2. Precompiled Headers
   - PCH.h already includes RE/Skyrim.h and SKSE/SKSE.h.
   - Do not redundantly re-include those headers in .cpp files.

3. Header Reference Locations
   - Primary project-local headers:
     H:/Nolvus Awakening/PROJECTS/MySkyrimPlugin/build/release/vcpkg_installed/x64-windows-static-md/include/
   - Global vcpkg package headers (fallback):
     C:/vcpkg/packages/commonlibsse-ng_x64-windows-static-md/include/
   - If you are unsure of a class member function, offset, or event signature, grep or read the corresponding header under the RE/ or SKSE/ directories before generating code. Never guess function signatures or member variable names.

4. Build & Deploy
   - Configure: cmake --preset release
   - Build: cmake --build H:/Nolvus Awakening/PROJECTS/MySkyrimPlugin/build/release
   - Output .dll is HelloWorld.dll.
   - If SKYRIM_MODS_FOLDER is set, the build automatically copies the .dll to <SKYRIM_MODS_FOLDER>/HelloWorld/SKSE/Plugins/.
   - If the automatic deploy is not configured, copy HelloWorld.dll from the build directory to the mod SKSE/Plugins/ folder manually.

5. Verification
   - After building, verify HelloWorld.dll exists in the build output or in the mod SKSE/Plugins/ folder.
   - Launch Skyrim via SKSE and check the ~ console or log file for expected output.

## When modifying code

- Prefer CommonLibSSE-NG abstractions over raw memory addresses.
- Use SKSE::GetMessagingInterface()->RegisterListener(...) for kDataLoaded and other SKSE message callbacks.
- Use RE::ConsoleLog::GetSingleton()->Print(...) for debug console output.
- Use SKSE::log::info(...) etc. for file logging when a logger is configured.
- Keep changes minimal and buildable; always run the build after editing and fix compiler errors by consulting the headers.
